@startuml user
title DeviceHub — src/user

package "Qt Network" {
  class QNetworkAccessManager
}

struct UserProfile {
  +login: QString
  +displayName: QString
  +avatarUrl: QString
}

class UserProfileClient {
  +fetchProfile(token: QString, login: QString)
  +updateOwnProfile(token: QString, displayName: QString, avatarUrl: QString)
  .. signals ..
  +profileReceived(profile: UserProfile)
  +profileUpdated(profile: UserProfile)
  +errorOccurred(message: QString)
}
UserProfileClient *-- QNetworkAccessManager : owns
UserProfileClient ..> UserProfile : emits
UserProfileClient ..> "user-service" : GET /users/{login}/profile,\nPATCH /users/me

note right of UserProfileClient
  Separate from AuthClient
  (auth-service) and ChatRestClient
  (chat-service) — user-service owns
  account/profile data, its own base
  URL (USER_SERVICE_URL). Async only,
  same pattern as the other REST
  clients — result comes back via
  signals, never blocks the GUI
  thread.

  updateOwnProfile() (issue #110)
  always writes to the token's own
  subject server-side — there's no
  way to pass a different login, so
  a caller can never edit someone
  else's profile through this class.
end note

@enduml
